Theme 1: Treat evals as an investment, not an obligation.
Recommendation: Before building an eval suite, assess whether the engineering effort will yield meaningful product improvements or whether those resources are better spent shipping new features.

Theme 2: Reserve rigorous evaluation for high-stakes, high-scale scenarios.
Recommendation: Prioritize formal evals where failures carry significant consequences or where AI performance is your core differentiator, and accept lighter-touch validation elsewhere.

Theme 3: Evaluate complex AI workflows step-by-step, not just end-to-end.
Recommendation: For multi-step processes like deep research or agentic pipelines, design evals that assess each intermediate stage so you can pinpoint exactly where quality breaks down.